1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,100
It took some work, but the renovations were finally completed.

2
00:00:06,760 --> 00:00:12,140
And with that, it was time to begin preparations for this world's wedding-slash-housewarming custom.

3
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:14,900
A.K.A. a reception.

4
00:00:15,820 --> 00:00:19,760
All right, Sylphie. Let's go over this guest list one last time.

5
00:00:20,080 --> 00:00:20,380
Right.

6
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:22,120
Here we go.

7
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:25,140
We have Alina, Lise, Zanoba, Julie, and Cliff.

8
00:00:26,040 --> 00:00:29,920
Linia, Persina, King Body, Vice Principal Genius, and Soldot.

9
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:33,320
Then Princess Ariel, her two attendants, and Luke.

10
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:37,700
I'd love to invite my family, but they're just too far away.

11
00:00:38,520 --> 00:00:40,200
I sent Paul a letter, at least.

12
00:00:40,720 --> 00:00:42,920
But who knows how long it will take to reach him.

13
00:00:43,360 --> 00:00:45,920
Hang on. You're still missing Nana Hoshi.

14
00:00:46,540 --> 00:00:48,580
Yeah, I'm not so sure she'd come.

15
00:00:48,580 --> 00:00:49,740
Well, I know she would.

16
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:51,400
Okay, I'll ask her and see.

17
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:55,740
But, uh, what if we do all this prep work and no one shows up?

18
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:59,300
I can promise you that Princess Ariel and Zanoba will be there.

19
00:00:59,720 --> 00:01:02,200
And I bet Linia and Persina will come as well.

20
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:05,500
They'd never refuse an invite from their boss, now would they?

21
00:01:05,840 --> 00:01:08,960
And I guess Cliff would come, since he specifically asked.

22
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:12,820
Personally, I'm hoping Alina Lise can join us.

23
00:01:14,260 --> 00:01:16,340
There's something I've been meaning to ask her.

24
00:01:16,880 --> 00:01:18,400
It's not really a big deal.

25
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:21,520
Really? I wonder what that could be.

26
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:24,560
I've barely even seen them in the same room together.

27
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:26,380
And I'll see you later.

28
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:38,740
Bye.

29
00:01:42,960 --> 00:01:44,100
Bye.

30
00:01:44,740 --> 00:01:45,320
Bye.

31
00:01:45,380 --> 00:01:47,240
Bye.

32
00:01:47,240 --> 00:01:47,620
Bye.

33
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:49,840
Bye.

34
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:49,900
Bye.

35
00:01:50,620 --> 00:01:51,520
Bye.

36
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:52,400
Bye.

37
00:01:52,640 --> 00:01:53,680
Bye.

38
00:01:53,720 --> 00:01:53,800
Bye.

39
00:01:53,820 --> 00:01:54,080
Bye.

40
00:02:57,030 --> 00:03:03,610
Now, with 10 plus guests attending this thing, we'll need to serve up quite a meal.

41
00:03:03,970 --> 00:03:05,810
So it's time for a little shopping trip.

42
00:03:07,090 --> 00:03:10,390
Before we get groceries, I'd like to buy you some new clothes.

43
00:03:10,750 --> 00:03:14,870
Good idea. I am kind of attached to these, but they've gotten pretty shabby.

44
00:03:15,890 --> 00:03:19,410
Clothes shopping it is. Dress me up however you like.

45
00:03:20,170 --> 00:03:21,570
I won't let you down.

46
00:03:22,570 --> 00:03:26,230
Would you be able to help us pick out a new set of mage's robes for him?

47
00:03:26,230 --> 00:03:31,350
Certainly. If I may ask, then, what particular schools of magic do you favor?

48
00:03:31,470 --> 00:03:34,270
Oh, uh, just water and earth, I suppose.

49
00:03:34,890 --> 00:03:41,210
Excellent. This one is quite water-resistant. This one is ideal for earth magic.

50
00:03:41,390 --> 00:03:43,670
I'm not sure. What do you like better, Sylphie?

51
00:03:44,190 --> 00:03:48,790
Actually, I'm fond of this one. And it's not too different from the one you have now.

52
00:03:49,090 --> 00:03:53,610
That robe is comprised largely of the pelt of the Lucky Rat from the Demon Continent.

53
00:03:53,610 --> 00:03:58,510
It's a Khazra design, highly resistant to both poison and acid.

54
00:03:58,670 --> 00:04:02,130
They do say names count for a lot. Guess we'll go with this.

55
00:04:04,350 --> 00:04:09,570
That is not a price I associate with clothes. Imported goods don't come cheap.

56
00:04:09,570 --> 00:04:14,650
If the name is what you like, good sir, do forgive me, but may I ask for yours?

57
00:04:14,990 --> 00:04:17,710
Oh, yeah. My name is Rudeus Greyrat.

58
00:04:18,230 --> 00:04:21,490
You don't say. I didn't realize you were a grey rat.

59
00:04:22,010 --> 00:04:25,470
Well, Lord Luke has been generous in his patronage to my shop.

60
00:04:25,710 --> 00:04:27,710
Please allow me to offer you a discount.

61
00:04:27,710 --> 00:04:54,050
We bought a lot of stuff today. Makes sense, though. Big house needs a lot of stuff.

62
00:04:54,050 --> 00:05:00,390
If money gets tight, I could go back to adventuring. Nah, and get myself killed.

63
00:05:03,050 --> 00:05:09,390
You're not worried about the money, are you? We will be fine, Rudy. I've been saving my wages from Princess Ariel.

64
00:05:09,570 --> 00:05:12,150
I know. It just makes me feel so useless.

65
00:05:12,950 --> 00:05:17,790
And leave the cooking to me, okay? I learned from your mom and Lilia, and I want to show off.

66
00:05:18,010 --> 00:05:20,050
Well, I wonder if it'll suit your tastes.

67
00:05:20,490 --> 00:05:22,550
For you, my love, I'd call charcoal delicious.

68
00:05:22,550 --> 00:05:27,890
Have a little faith. I mean, honestly, who do you think I spent all that time learning to cook for?

69
00:05:28,070 --> 00:05:33,390
Oh, Sylphiette, you're such a perfect bride. I can't help but feel nervous that I'm not worthy of you.

70
00:05:33,990 --> 00:05:37,990
Of course you are, silly. You're my ideal husband, too, you know.

71
00:05:41,530 --> 00:05:43,090
Rudeus, I love you.

72
00:05:43,090 --> 00:05:46,650
Uh-oh.

73
00:05:48,650 --> 00:05:50,530
Hey, hey, hey, hey, what are you?

74
00:05:52,150 --> 00:05:52,830
Oh, God.

75
00:05:54,090 --> 00:05:54,650
Jeez.

76
00:05:54,650 --> 00:06:05,970
A few days later, it was time for the reception.

77
00:06:06,910 --> 00:06:09,650
We picked a day during our monthly break, noon sharp.

78
00:06:10,290 --> 00:06:13,610
Genius excused himself, and Soldot said he was too busy.

79
00:06:13,610 --> 00:06:17,290
Badigati said he'd come, which surprised me.

80
00:06:18,070 --> 00:06:20,270
The other 11 invites were all accepted.

81
00:06:21,890 --> 00:06:24,810
Yes, even Nana Hoshi came to join us.

82
00:06:26,890 --> 00:06:30,030
Well, this is rare. Weird to see you outside your tower.

83
00:06:30,350 --> 00:06:31,790
You're the one who invited me.

84
00:06:32,170 --> 00:06:34,210
Yep, and I'm very glad you could make it.

85
00:06:34,490 --> 00:06:36,530
We've got some potato chips and stuff for you.

86
00:06:36,750 --> 00:06:38,070
Really? Did you make them?

87
00:06:38,070 --> 00:06:41,450
Of course, because thanks to you, we were able to get a hold of cooking oil.

88
00:06:41,850 --> 00:06:42,690
Where are they?

89
00:06:43,150 --> 00:06:44,830
Rudy, everything's ready.

90
00:06:45,730 --> 00:06:49,070
Oh, and we told our guests the truth about silent fits.

91
00:06:50,010 --> 00:06:52,830
Okay, now we're just waiting on Badigati.

92
00:06:53,230 --> 00:06:56,530
People who live for millennia have no concept of how time passes.

93
00:06:57,290 --> 00:07:00,430
You can probably expect them to arrive a month or so from now.

94
00:07:01,210 --> 00:07:03,250
Yeah, best to go ahead and get started then.

95
00:07:04,010 --> 00:07:05,110
Sorry, Badigati.

96
00:07:08,070 --> 00:07:16,710
You can do it.

97
00:07:18,790 --> 00:07:20,630
Thank you all for joining us today.

98
00:07:21,090 --> 00:07:23,370
We know you're busy and we're so glad you came.

99
00:07:23,710 --> 00:07:28,970
The occasion is no secret, but, um, just to say it officially, Sylphie and I...

100
00:07:28,970 --> 00:07:32,230
Enter the Demon King, Badigati, with us a bang!

101
00:07:34,930 --> 00:07:37,090
Badigati, you're a little late, you know.

102
00:07:37,090 --> 00:07:39,030
Ah, that is where you are wrong.

103
00:07:39,430 --> 00:07:44,570
Among my people, royals arrive when least expected, so as to astound and astonish the masses.

104
00:07:45,010 --> 00:07:46,530
Thus, I am right on time.

105
00:07:46,750 --> 00:07:47,510
You're joking.

106
00:07:47,870 --> 00:07:49,070
No, it's true.

107
00:07:49,290 --> 00:07:52,230
I went quite out of my way on your account, young gray rat.

108
00:07:52,410 --> 00:07:53,530
You ought to be grateful.

109
00:07:55,050 --> 00:07:56,530
Sure, thank you, sire.

110
00:07:56,530 --> 00:08:03,370
Now then, as I was saying, thank you for taking time out of your busy lives for us.

111
00:08:03,710 --> 00:08:06,790
And as you know, Sylphiet and I are to be married.

112
00:08:07,430 --> 00:08:10,910
We know that we're still young, but we hope for a fruitful life together.

113
00:08:11,870 --> 00:08:18,010
Those of you gathered today have been especially close to us during our time here, so, um...

114
00:08:18,010 --> 00:08:21,630
Ah, crap, that was way too stiff and formal, wasn't it?

115
00:08:22,070 --> 00:08:23,330
I'm making this awkward.

116
00:08:24,290 --> 00:08:26,930
No need to stand on ceremony, young man.

117
00:08:27,250 --> 00:08:29,230
You two love each other, do you not?

118
00:08:29,490 --> 00:08:32,210
Simply allow us all to celebrate that love together.

119
00:08:32,210 --> 00:08:39,210
Hmm.

120
00:08:44,290 --> 00:08:45,170
Basically that.

121
00:08:45,630 --> 00:08:48,030
We're starting a life together, so...

122
00:08:48,030 --> 00:08:49,790
We hope you'll all stay a part of it.

123
00:08:49,970 --> 00:08:50,270
Thanks!

124
00:08:51,150 --> 00:08:54,230
And now, a toast to the young couple's future!

125
00:08:54,710 --> 00:08:55,650
Cheers, everyone!

126
00:08:56,230 --> 00:08:57,190
Cheers, everyone!

127
00:09:02,210 --> 00:09:24,330
Sylphie, congratulations!

128
00:09:24,850 --> 00:09:26,210
Thank you so very much!

129
00:09:26,530 --> 00:09:30,710
Now pray tell, do your home and husband meet your expectations, my dear?

130
00:09:30,710 --> 00:09:32,870
Both better than I ever dared to dream.

131
00:09:33,410 --> 00:09:35,330
Did I tell you we even have a bath here?

132
00:09:35,470 --> 00:09:40,030
You know, we could arrange for you to take a year off from being my bodyguard if you would like that.

133
00:09:40,590 --> 00:09:43,710
Um, not yet, but if we have children...

134
00:09:44,470 --> 00:09:46,630
Please don't tease me, your highness!

135
00:09:47,490 --> 00:09:50,990
Well, I figure you still don't like me that much, but...

136
00:09:50,990 --> 00:09:52,190
Let's try to get along.

137
00:09:52,830 --> 00:09:55,110
I know I don't have any hang-ups...

138
00:09:55,110 --> 00:09:55,750
Sounds good.

139
00:09:56,710 --> 00:09:57,830
I'd like that, Luke.

140
00:10:00,710 --> 00:10:04,910
Hello, Grandmaster and Mrs. Grandmaster.

141
00:10:05,230 --> 00:10:06,790
Thank you for inviting me today.

142
00:10:06,990 --> 00:10:09,930
And from the bottom of our hearts, warm congratulations.

143
00:10:10,630 --> 00:10:11,950
Thank you both, really.

144
00:10:12,290 --> 00:10:13,290
And you, fair lady.

145
00:10:13,730 --> 00:10:16,450
How could I have mistaken my master's wife for a man?

146
00:10:17,130 --> 00:10:19,530
I hope you can forgive my rudeness all this time.

147
00:10:19,650 --> 00:10:20,370
Oh, gosh.

148
00:10:20,550 --> 00:10:21,850
You don't have to bow to me.

149
00:10:22,570 --> 00:10:24,250
Rudy mistook me for a man before.

150
00:10:24,590 --> 00:10:25,270
Twice even.

151
00:10:25,670 --> 00:10:25,990
Right?

152
00:10:26,990 --> 00:10:28,450
Embarrassing as it is to admit it.

153
00:10:28,450 --> 00:10:29,890
Yes, yes, I did.

154
00:10:30,610 --> 00:10:34,630
Cubans don't normally stand around and yap at each other in the middle of a meal, do they?

155
00:10:34,770 --> 00:10:36,250
Yeah, mind your manners.

156
00:10:36,610 --> 00:10:38,470
She sat around a mouthful of food.

157
00:10:38,590 --> 00:10:40,510
Thank you both so much for coming today.

158
00:10:40,870 --> 00:10:45,070
Absolutely, like I was ever going to miss watching Silent Fitz and the Boss tie the knot.

159
00:10:45,150 --> 00:10:47,030
Yeah, I always figured Fitz was a woman.

160
00:10:47,490 --> 00:10:49,710
Pretty obvious to anyone within smell and distance.

161
00:10:50,330 --> 00:10:53,370
Anyway, it's always good to see strong people get together, meow.

162
00:10:53,370 --> 00:10:54,630
That's for sure.

163
00:10:54,990 --> 00:10:57,770
Having strong children brings tranquility to the tribe.

164
00:10:58,470 --> 00:11:00,370
Sure, that's one way to put it.

165
00:11:00,550 --> 00:11:01,010
Why not?

166
00:11:01,010 --> 00:11:06,770
Congrats.

167
00:11:07,330 --> 00:11:08,010
Thank you.

168
00:11:10,010 --> 00:11:11,770
Wait, Nana Hoshi?

169
00:11:12,230 --> 00:11:13,370
Can I ask you something?

170
00:11:14,010 --> 00:11:14,870
I suppose.

171
00:11:15,430 --> 00:11:19,050
One time, you said that you and Rudy come from the same place.

172
00:11:19,550 --> 00:11:21,270
Tell me, what do you mean?

173
00:11:21,270 --> 00:11:32,170
Since he can speak my language, I just assumed.

174
00:11:39,730 --> 00:11:45,190
Oh God, grant them eternal love and gift them with bountiful fortune.

175
00:11:46,230 --> 00:11:50,330
Best prayer I've got, I humbly bless your marriage.

176
00:11:50,330 --> 00:11:52,010
Thank you so much.

177
00:11:53,190 --> 00:11:55,130
Rudeus, your manhood is back.

178
00:11:55,430 --> 00:11:55,870
Congratulations.

179
00:11:56,850 --> 00:12:00,610
I would have preferred to hear it from you, so don't hesitate to tell me next time.

180
00:12:00,870 --> 00:12:04,890
Why, so you could ask if I was telling the truth and jump my bones to make me prove it?

181
00:12:04,990 --> 00:12:05,690
No thanks.

182
00:12:06,070 --> 00:12:07,110
That's not fair.

183
00:12:07,350 --> 00:12:08,590
Remember what I told you?

184
00:12:08,770 --> 00:12:12,470
I have no intention of becoming the daughter-in-law of Mr. Paul Greyrat.

185
00:12:12,930 --> 00:12:15,550
Sylphiette, I'm happy for you, dear.

186
00:12:15,770 --> 00:12:17,030
Thanks, that means a lot.

187
00:12:17,030 --> 00:12:24,030
And I wish you both happy, happiness with all my...

188
00:12:24,030 --> 00:12:32,410
I'm so sorry.

189
00:12:32,850 --> 00:12:34,490
I don't know what's come over me.

190
00:12:36,250 --> 00:12:37,030
What's wrong?

191
00:12:37,290 --> 00:12:37,990
Are you okay?

192
00:12:37,990 --> 00:12:45,030
Um, Alina Lise, do you feel sad because there's a chance you could be my grandma?

193
00:12:48,710 --> 00:12:54,070
According to my father, my grandmother went on many adventures with Paul Greyrat.

194
00:12:54,070 --> 00:12:55,930
No, that's not true.

195
00:12:56,230 --> 00:12:59,030
I doubt any grandmother of yours would be a whore like me.

196
00:12:59,410 --> 00:13:02,650
I heard my dad got chased out of the Great Forest because of it.

197
00:13:02,890 --> 00:13:04,950
Apparently, he had trouble marrying, too.

198
00:13:05,250 --> 00:13:07,830
I was hoping there'd be a connection.

199
00:13:08,510 --> 00:13:10,870
What little he told me seemed to have fit you well.

200
00:13:11,350 --> 00:13:12,530
I thought it might be you.

201
00:13:12,970 --> 00:13:14,070
Well, you see...

202
00:13:14,070 --> 00:13:16,070
Oh, uh...

203
00:13:16,070 --> 00:13:16,950
Oh, uh...

204
00:13:16,950 --> 00:13:18,150
Well, please forgive me.

205
00:13:18,330 --> 00:13:18,970
I'm sorry.

206
00:13:19,550 --> 00:13:20,190
They're related?

207
00:13:21,110 --> 00:13:26,750
I'm starting to think it's not a coincidence that the pendant Sylphie made me look like Alina Lises.

208
00:13:27,570 --> 00:13:29,950
And yeah, their faces are so similar.

209
00:13:30,650 --> 00:13:31,410
Master Cliff?

210
00:13:31,590 --> 00:13:31,850
Yes?

211
00:13:32,150 --> 00:13:32,750
What is it?

212
00:13:33,090 --> 00:13:36,310
Could you help Alina Lise to a room upstairs so she can have some privacy?

213
00:13:37,150 --> 00:13:37,490
Yes.

214
00:13:37,810 --> 00:13:38,430
Right away.

215
00:13:38,430 --> 00:13:42,710
I think we should wait to have this conversation until she's had some time to rest.

216
00:13:42,930 --> 00:13:44,170
Yes, of course.

217
00:13:45,090 --> 00:13:46,470
Rudeus, I...

218
00:13:46,470 --> 00:13:51,350
I know who I can be, but Lass didn't have the same predilections.

219
00:13:51,810 --> 00:13:54,810
It's true, and neither does his daughter Sylphie.

220
00:13:54,970 --> 00:13:55,930
So please...

221
00:13:55,930 --> 00:13:57,730
You don't have anything to worry about.

222
00:13:58,250 --> 00:14:01,190
I would never leave Sylphiette just because she's related to you.

223
00:14:01,710 --> 00:14:02,170
But...

224
00:14:02,170 --> 00:14:07,890
Not to mention, if I were you, I'd be a lot more concerned about the fact that you're about to be related to Paul.

225
00:14:08,670 --> 00:14:12,510
Rudy, you picked a hell of a time to be a wisecrack.

226
00:14:21,550 --> 00:14:23,890
Bye, Meow. Don't forget to be happy.

227
00:14:24,570 --> 00:14:27,490
Man, you really are the boss of the school. No butts about it.

228
00:14:27,810 --> 00:14:29,430
I can't wait for the next term.

229
00:14:30,170 --> 00:14:33,370
I should get going. I'll have more experiments for you tomorrow.

230
00:14:35,470 --> 00:14:38,010
Perhaps... I could come and use your bath from time to time?

231
00:14:38,430 --> 00:14:40,670
Oh, Master, are you okay?

232
00:14:41,070 --> 00:14:44,130
Uh, it appears I got a bit too carried away.

233
00:14:44,490 --> 00:14:47,050
Those are weak words, even for a blessed child.

234
00:14:48,050 --> 00:14:49,370
Ow! Ow!

235
00:14:56,110 --> 00:14:58,310
Hey, Cliff, could Grandma...

236
00:14:58,310 --> 00:15:02,350
I mean, Alina, Lisa and I have a moment to speak in private, please?

237
00:15:02,730 --> 00:15:03,470
That okay?

238
00:15:03,470 --> 00:15:06,270
Yes, I'll be fine.

239
00:15:09,610 --> 00:15:11,370
Thank you, Cliff, Rudy.

240
00:15:18,170 --> 00:15:20,590
Hey, Rodius, will they be alright?

241
00:15:20,590 --> 00:15:24,510
If not, you and I are here to smooth things over.

242
00:15:28,430 --> 00:15:31,670
Mr. Greyrat, thank you for inviting us here today.

243
00:15:32,230 --> 00:15:34,110
Please, thank you for joining us.

244
00:15:34,450 --> 00:15:36,670
Not to pry, but what's become of Sylphie?

245
00:15:37,070 --> 00:15:39,170
She's speaking with Alina Lisa at the moment.

246
00:15:39,950 --> 00:15:42,270
Ah, yes, I see. What perfect timing.

247
00:15:42,270 --> 00:15:45,630
May I steal you for a few minutes, then?

248
00:15:49,550 --> 00:15:52,670
Mr. Greyrat, this may sound impertinent,

249
00:15:53,190 --> 00:15:55,750
but could you be troubled to agree to duel Luke?

250
00:15:56,010 --> 00:15:56,630
No magic.

251
00:15:57,190 --> 00:15:58,750
Strictly sword against sword.

252
00:16:00,950 --> 00:16:03,550
Rest assured, this is all in good fun.

253
00:16:03,870 --> 00:16:05,590
Oh, sure. All in good fun.

254
00:16:06,130 --> 00:16:08,570
Then you wouldn't mind if we use fake swords, right?

255
00:16:08,570 --> 00:16:12,290
If you'd like to conjure a sword with magic, I wouldn't object.

256
00:16:12,670 --> 00:16:15,170
Yeah, but even if I were to do that,

257
00:16:15,310 --> 00:16:17,430
Luke could still slice me clean in two.

258
00:16:17,830 --> 00:16:18,690
I don't get it.

259
00:16:19,050 --> 00:16:20,850
Why are they trying to rush me into a duel?

260
00:16:21,590 --> 00:16:23,990
Have I done something to offend you, princess?

261
00:16:24,750 --> 00:16:25,210
Hardly.

262
00:16:25,730 --> 00:16:28,110
It's just a challenge you're free to refuse.

263
00:16:28,950 --> 00:16:29,390
However,

264
00:16:30,150 --> 00:16:32,310
I do hope you're inclined to accept.

265
00:16:33,210 --> 00:16:33,690
Rudeus.

266
00:16:34,330 --> 00:16:34,810
Accept.

267
00:16:34,810 --> 00:16:39,170
Very well.

268
00:16:54,530 --> 00:16:54,850
Begin!

269
00:17:01,850 --> 00:17:02,930
You got lucky!

270
00:17:02,990 --> 00:17:03,110
No!

271
00:17:04,810 --> 00:17:07,110
We're done.

272
00:17:08,350 --> 00:17:08,990
Enough!

273
00:17:11,570 --> 00:17:12,490
Come on!

274
00:17:13,810 --> 00:17:14,490
Elemois.

275
00:17:14,850 --> 00:17:15,690
A healing spell.

276
00:17:17,370 --> 00:17:18,330
How's your hand?

277
00:17:18,890 --> 00:17:19,430
Are you alright?

278
00:17:20,290 --> 00:17:21,530
Yeah, I'm fine.

279
00:17:23,530 --> 00:17:25,190
Take good care of Sylvie.

280
00:17:25,830 --> 00:17:26,490
I mean it.

281
00:17:26,890 --> 00:17:28,270
On my life, of course.

282
00:17:28,850 --> 00:17:33,270
But is there a reason you chose today of all days to challenge me to a duel?

283
00:17:33,270 --> 00:17:35,550
There's not much to it, really.

284
00:17:36,550 --> 00:17:38,190
Sylvie is very dear to us.

285
00:17:38,930 --> 00:17:42,730
We've bonded through the course of our perilous travail, so forgive us, please.

286
00:17:43,110 --> 00:17:46,450
Consider this duel a matter of personal pride and assurances.

287
00:17:46,450 --> 00:17:50,470
I guess they wanted to find out if they can trust me with Sylvie's life.

288
00:17:50,910 --> 00:17:51,910
Can't say I blame them.

289
00:17:51,910 --> 00:17:55,230
I will make my return to Asura someday.

290
00:17:55,830 --> 00:17:59,170
When I do, I will claim the throne, or die trying.

291
00:17:59,170 --> 00:18:01,850
It is my right, my duty.

292
00:18:01,850 --> 00:18:07,130
But Sylvie has no obligation to accompany me.

293
00:18:07,630 --> 00:18:09,950
She is neither royalty nor nobility.

294
00:18:10,550 --> 00:18:13,730
We were merely brought together by the mass teleportation.

295
00:18:13,730 --> 00:18:16,730
Moreover, it's not my duty to presume on her.

296
00:18:17,550 --> 00:18:20,610
So it's time I let her go to choose her own path.

297
00:18:21,390 --> 00:18:22,970
It won't take long, you see.

298
00:18:23,330 --> 00:18:27,190
Once she has a child, her desire to join us should fade of its own accord.

299
00:18:27,890 --> 00:18:32,990
If she fails to move on, I'm leaving it up to you to step in and talk some sense into her.

300
00:18:32,990 --> 00:18:35,110
That's a big ask.

301
00:18:35,570 --> 00:18:37,510
I'm also in the princess's debt.

302
00:18:38,150 --> 00:18:41,650
If I'm not careful, I'll end up wanting to tag along too.

303
00:18:41,750 --> 00:18:42,830
Make no mistake.

304
00:18:43,350 --> 00:18:48,990
If you fail to give our Sylvie the life she deserves, we will take her back, no question.

305
00:18:50,370 --> 00:18:52,030
You have my word, princess.

306
00:19:02,990 --> 00:19:13,190
Oh, Rudy, where's the princess?

307
00:19:13,650 --> 00:19:15,410
I'm afraid you just missed her.

308
00:19:15,810 --> 00:19:18,390
So Luke challenged Rudeus to a duel out of nowhere.

309
00:19:18,850 --> 00:19:20,390
But Rudeus didn't back down.

310
00:19:20,670 --> 00:19:21,870
He won no problem.

311
00:19:23,330 --> 00:19:24,170
Did you?

312
00:19:24,850 --> 00:19:27,630
Uh, yeah, I think that about sums it up.

313
00:19:27,950 --> 00:19:29,830
Were you two able to finish your talk?

314
00:19:30,130 --> 00:19:30,430
Yep.

315
00:19:30,430 --> 00:19:37,210
It sounds like Alina Lise is Sylvie's grandmother after all.

316
00:19:38,270 --> 00:19:41,550
Between her curse and her personality, she was never far from trouble.

317
00:19:42,110 --> 00:19:45,350
So even when she had kids, she kept her real identity a secret.

318
00:19:45,910 --> 00:19:48,910
And once they got old enough to fend for themselves, she disappeared.

319
00:19:49,450 --> 00:19:50,430
All to protect them.

320
00:19:53,150 --> 00:19:56,570
She pegged Sylvie as a descendant the moment she laid eyes on her.

321
00:19:56,570 --> 00:19:59,170
But revealing herself never crossed her mind.

322
00:20:00,430 --> 00:20:05,010
Until she saw Sylvie beaming with joy and became flooded with emotions.

323
00:20:05,670 --> 00:20:07,810
Rudeus, I have a confession.

324
00:20:08,390 --> 00:20:09,050
It's Lise.

325
00:20:09,630 --> 00:20:11,750
She's not the person I thought she was.

326
00:20:12,330 --> 00:20:12,870
Oh, yeah?

327
00:20:13,450 --> 00:20:13,810
And?

328
00:20:14,190 --> 00:20:15,710
Finally disillusioned, huh?

329
00:20:16,070 --> 00:20:18,210
His crush not only has kids, but grandkids.

330
00:20:19,350 --> 00:20:21,070
That had hit me pretty hard, too.

331
00:20:21,070 --> 00:20:24,010
She's more sensitive than I could ever know.

332
00:20:24,610 --> 00:20:25,290
The poor thing.

333
00:20:26,010 --> 00:20:27,850
I swear I'll lift her curse.

334
00:20:29,430 --> 00:20:33,350
But to make sure I get the job done right, I'd like your help.

335
00:20:33,350 --> 00:20:38,630
So you didn't feel disillusioned after finding out who she really was?

336
00:20:38,970 --> 00:20:39,450
Disillusioned?

337
00:20:39,630 --> 00:20:40,530
Of course not.

338
00:20:40,890 --> 00:20:41,970
Why would you even think that?

339
00:20:42,610 --> 00:20:49,690
As my faith teaches, no matter her circumstances, whether our ideals clash, I have a duty to make

340
00:20:49,690 --> 00:20:52,050
the woman who loves me as happy as she can be.

341
00:20:52,910 --> 00:20:55,730
Because I've fallen in love with her as well.

342
00:21:00,790 --> 00:21:01,870
I understand.

343
00:21:02,610 --> 00:21:05,330
If there's any way I can help, allow me to assist.

344
00:21:09,670 --> 00:21:10,650
Rude, please.

345
00:21:10,650 --> 00:21:12,170
I thought we were friends now.

346
00:21:12,470 --> 00:21:13,610
Stop being so formal.

347
00:21:14,370 --> 00:21:15,370
I refuse.

348
00:21:29,230 --> 00:21:30,890
Rudy, I've been thinking.

349
00:21:31,250 --> 00:21:32,630
I'd like to grow my hair out.

350
00:21:33,270 --> 00:21:34,750
Are you quite certain?

351
00:21:34,790 --> 00:21:36,590
You are always being so formal.

352
00:21:37,070 --> 00:21:39,490
My hair isn't green anymore, so I might as well.

353
00:21:39,490 --> 00:21:43,170
I'll work hard so your love for me stays strong.

354
00:21:43,370 --> 00:21:44,170
I promise.

355
00:21:45,090 --> 00:21:46,690
How did I get so lucky?

356
00:21:47,010 --> 00:21:48,310
She's gonna make me cry.

357
00:21:49,510 --> 00:21:52,250
I'll work hard to keep her love for me strong, too.

358
00:21:52,690 --> 00:21:53,370
Hey, Sylphie.

359
00:21:53,670 --> 00:21:54,910
Thanks for everything today.

360
00:21:55,430 --> 00:21:56,610
Oh, of course.

361
00:21:56,830 --> 00:21:57,470
Thank you.

362
00:23:36,060 --> 00:23:40,060
La-ya-la-ya-la

